WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.910
Two essays answer the same
question on the design argument.

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.820
One stays strictly inside that topic.

3
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:09.740
The other reaches into
another part of the course:

4
00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.800
Charles Darwin's theory
and what it changed.

5
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:17.860
So when does reaching beyond the topic
in the question earn the highest marks?

6
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.090
In this mission, you'll
sort links into four kinds,

7
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.090
from shared ideas to clear contrasts.

8
00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.760
Then you'll test which pairs of
arguments really share a method,

9
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.810
and which only look alike.

10
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:34.250
Your mission: find out when reaching
beyond the topic lifts an answer,

11
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.400
and when it does not.
